# macOS HIG — Savitar 2

Full reference: [docs/HIG.md](../../docs/HIG.md) (UI requirements). Implementation backlog: [docs/Stories.md](../../docs/Stories.md).

## Settings window checklist

- One modeless **Settings** window; **Settings…** in app menu (**⌘,**)
- Toolbar panes: Startup, Input & Display, **Colors**, Audio, Updates, Speech
- **No** Save / Cancel / Apply — changes apply and persist immediately
- Close button only; `fitContentSize` per pane (Colors/Speech may grow the window)
- `NSToolbar` with `.preference` style; window title = active pane name
- Dismiss with **Escape** or **⌘+.**
- **Edit → ANSI Colors…** and **Audio → Speech Settings…** deep-link to panes
- Use `NSWindow.configureAsSettingsWindow()` and `fitContentSize(_:centerIfNeeded:)`

## Other surfaces

- **World Settings** → modal sheet on world document (OK/Cancel); not app Settings
- **Events** / **World Picker** → modeless utility windows; see HIG.md for open chrome items (Stories 6–7)
- Gray out unsupported options with a tooltip (do not hide)

## When adding UI

1. Check [docs/HIG.md](../../docs/HIG.md) for requirements
2. Check [docs/Stories.md](../../docs/Stories.md) if tracking new work
3. Match existing AppKit patterns in `client/Savitar2/src/views/`
4. Prefer system controls, Auto Layout, and standard shortcuts
